{
  "_comment": [
    "A default profile: every Ethernet interface gets DHCPv4, link-local when",
    "nobody answers, and its DNS servers from the lease.",
    "",
    "Separate from the service definition on purpose. Starting netd and",
    "deciding that unknown wired interfaces should join whatever network they",
    "are plugged into are two decisions; a hardened image may want the first",
    "without the second and ship profiles naming its interfaces instead.",
    "",
    "Priority 10 is low, so any profile an operator adds at the default 100",
    "wins over it without needing to know this one exists."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\System" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Network" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Profiles" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Profiles\\ethernet",
      "values": [
        { "name": "Priority", "type": "dword", "data": 10 },
        { "name": "Managed", "type": "dword", "data": 1 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Profiles\\ethernet\\Match",
      "values": [
        { "name": "Type", "type": "sz", "data": "ether" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Profiles\\ethernet\\Address",
      "values": [
        { "name": "DHCP4", "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "LinkLocal", "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "OnLeaseExpiry", "type": "sz", "data": "Drop" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Profiles\\ethernet\\DNS",
      "values": [
        { "name": "UseFromDHCP", "type": "dword", "data": 1 }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
